---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = 'How to Apply for China Tourist Visa (L-Type) 2026: A Step-by-Step Guide';
const description = 'Complete step-by-step guide for applying to a Chinese L-type tourist visa in 2026. Official documents, COVA online form, appointment booking, fees, and FAQ.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} lang="fr">
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-8 not-prose">
      <a href="/fr/visa/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-gray-400 hover:text-gray-700 transition no-underline group">
        <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 transition-transform group-hover:-translate-x-0.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"/>
        </svg>
        Back to Prepare
      </a>
    </nav>
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="mb-12">
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-3">📋 Tourist Visa</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-4 leading-tight">
        How to Apply for China Tourist Visa (L-Type) 2026
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-6">A complete step-by-step guide to getting your Chinese tourist visa.</p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-gray-500">
        <span>📅 Last updated: June 2026</span>
        <span>⏱️ 8 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Quick Answer Box -->
    <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-50 to-indigo-50 border-l-4 border-blue-500 rounded-r-2xl p-8 mb-12 not-prose">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-blue-900 mb-4">🎯 Quick Answer</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-blue-800 leading-relaxed">
        <strong>Apply online via <a href="http://cova.mfa.gov.cn/" class="text-blue-700 underline">COVA</a>, then visit your local Visa Application Center in person.</strong> You'll need a valid passport, completed form, photo, travel itinerary, and visa fee. Processing takes 4-5 business days typically.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-8 not-prose">
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 mb-1 font-semibold">Official portals:</p>
      <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 space-y-1">
        <li>📋 <a href="http://cova.mfa.gov.cn/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">COVA Online Form</a> — Fill in your visa application</li>
        <li>📖 <a href="https://consular.mfa.gov.cn/VISA/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Consular Affairs Visa Guide</a> — Official step-by-step guidance</li>
        <li>📍 <a href="https://www.visaforchina.cn" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visa Application Centers</a> — Find your local center & book appointments</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Main Content -->
    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">
        If you've read our <a href="/fr/visa/visa-guide/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">China Visa Types Complete Guide</a> and confirmed you need an L-type tourist visa — here's exactly how to apply, step by step, using the official online system.
      </p>

      <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">🛂</span> Do You Need an L-Type Visa?
      </h2>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-4">
        <strong>You need an L-type tourist visa if:</strong>
      </p>

      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700 mb-6">
        <li>Your passport is NOT from one of the <a href="/fr/visa/visa-free/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">visa-free countries</a></li>
        <li>You do NOT have a qualifying third-country itinerary for <a href="/fr/visa/transit-240/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">240-hour transit</a></li>
        <li>You plan to visit China for tourism (not work, study, or business)</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
        L-type visas are typically issued for 30, 60, or 90 days per entry. Multiple-entry options are available depending on your nationality and visa history.
      </p>

      <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">📄</span> What Documents Do You Need?
      </h2>

      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
        Based on the <a href="https://cs.mfa.gov.cn/wgrlh/lhqz/cjwdn_660600/201407/t20140717_961493.shtml" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official Chinese Consular Affairs Website</a>, here's what you must prepare:
      </p>

      <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-8 not-prose">
        <ul class="space-y-4">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-lg">✅</span>
            <div><strong class="text-gray-900">Valid passport</strong><br/><span class="text-sm text-gray-600">At least 6 months validity + 2 blank visa pages</span></div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-lg">✅</span>
            <div><strong class="text-gray-900">COVA Online Application Form</strong><br/><span class="text-sm text-gray-600">Completed and printed with a valid barcode</span></div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-lg">✅</span>
            <div><strong class="text-gray-900">Passport photo</strong><br/><span class="text-sm text-gray-600">48mm × 33mm, white background, taken within 6 months</span></div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-lg">✅</span>
            <div><strong class="text-gray-900">Round trip flight booking</strong><br/><span class="text-sm text-gray-600">Confirmed itinerary showing entry and exit dates</span></div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-lg">✅</span>
            <div><strong class="text-gray-900">Hotel bookings</strong><br/><span class="text-sm text-gray-600">For your entire stay, or a letter of invitation from your host</span></div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-lg">✅</span>
            <div><strong class="text-gray-900">Proof of sufficient funds</strong><br/><span class="text-sm text-gray-600">Bank statements from the last 3 months</span></div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-lg">✅</span>
            <div><strong class="text-gray-900">Copies of previous Chinese visas</strong><br/><span class="text-sm text-gray-600">If you've visited before</span></div>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">📝</span> Step-by-Step Procédure de Demande
      </h2>

      <div class="space-y-6 mb-8 not-prose">
        <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-3">
            <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-blue-600 text-white text-lg font-bold flex items-center justify-center">1</span>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Fill in the COVA Online Form</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-3">Visit <a href="http://cova.mfa.gov.cn/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline" target="_blank">cova.mfa.gov.cn</a> and complete the online visa application. The form asks for personal details, travel history, passport info, and trip itinerary.</p>
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-4">
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 font-semibold mb-1">💡 Tips for COVA:</p>
            <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 space-y-1">
              <li>• Save your application ID — you'll need it to retrieve your form</li>
              <li>• Print the final form with the barcode visible on the last page</li>
              <li>• Some consulates only require you to fill in COVA, while others also require an appointment — check your local center's instructions</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-green-50 border border-green-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-3">
            <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-green-600 text-white text-lg font-bold flex items-center justify-center">2</span>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Book an Appointment</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-3">Visit <a href="https://www.visaforchina.cn" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline" target="_blank">visaforchina.cn</a> to book your appointment at the nearest Visa Application Center. Many centers require appointments, and walk-ins may not be accepted.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-purple-50 border border-purple-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-3">
            <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-purple-600 text-white text-lg font-bold flex items-center justify-center">3</span>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Prepare Your Documents</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-gray-700">Gather all required documents listed above. Make copies of everything — the center may keep originals and only return your passport with the visa.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-orange-50 border border-orange-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-3">
            <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-orange-600 text-white text-lg font-bold flex items-center justify-center">4</span>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Visit the Visa Application Center</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-3">Bring your documents in person. You'll submit them, get your fingerprints taken (for most applicants), and pay the fee.</p>
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-4">
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600"><strong>Fee:</strong> Typically $30–$100 USD depending on nationality, number of entries, and processing speed.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-teal-50 border border-teal-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-3">
            <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-teal-600 text-white text-lg font-bold flex items-center justify-center">5</span>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Wait for Processing</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-gray-700">Standard processing takes 4–5 business days. Expedited service (2–3 days) may be available at an additional fee. You can track your application status online.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-3">
            <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-red-600 text-white text-lg font-bold flex items-center justify-center">6</span>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Collect Your Passport</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-gray-700">Return to the center with your receipt to collect your passport with the visa. Some centers offer mail delivery.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">💡</span> Tips for a Smooth Application
      </h2>

      <div class="bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-5 rounded-r-xl mb-6 not-prose">
        <p class="text-yellow-900"><strong>Apply early:</strong> Start at least 4-6 weeks before your trip. Processing delays happen, and you don't want to be stressed.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-5 rounded-r-xl mb-6 not-prose">
        <p class="text-yellow-900"><strong>Double-check everything:</strong> Incomplete forms are the #1 reason for delays. One missing signature or wrong date can set you back a week.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-5 rounded-r-xl mb-6 not-prose">
        <p class="text-yellow-900"><strong>Be honest:</strong> Any incorrect information on your application can lead to rejection or future visa issues.</p>
      </div>

      <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">❓</span> Frequently Asked Questions
      </h2>

      <div class="space-y-6 mb-8 not-prose">
        <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can I apply by mail?</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">Most applicants must apply in person at a Visa Application Center. Some countries allow third-party submission, but you generally need to visit the center at least once. Check your local center's website for specific rules.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How long is the visa valid?</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">Typically 3 months from the date of issue. You must enter China within this window. The duration of stay (e.g., 30 days) starts counting from the day you enter China.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can I extend my visa in China?</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">Yes, you can apply for a visa extension at the local Public Security Bureau (PSB) Exit-Entry Administration office in China. Extensions are typically granted for up to 30 additional days.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">What if my visa is rejected?</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">Visa rejection is relatively rare for straightforward tourist applications. If rejected, you'll generally receive a reason. You can reapply after addressing the issue. Common reasons include incomplete documentation or insufficient funds.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Sources -->
    <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 not-prose mt-12">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">📚 Sources</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-2">
        <li><a href="https://www.visaforchina.cn/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline text-sm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">China Visa Application Service Center</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://consular.mfa.gov.cn/VISA/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline text-sm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">China Online VISA Application (COVA)</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Related Guides -->
    <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-8 not-prose mt-12">
      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">📚 Related Guides</h3>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href="/fr/visa/visa-guide/" class="block bg-white rounded-xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition border border-gray-100">
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">China Visa Types Complete Guide</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">All visa options explained</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/fr/visa/visa-free/" class="block bg-white rounded-xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition border border-gray-100">
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">China Visa-Free Countries List (2026)</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">See if your passport qualifies</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>